Subject: gl: GLSL 1.20 texture lookups without a bias argument

The 3D shaders (terrain, decals, models, buttons) sample through a macro that is texture2D(tex, uv,
bias) on GLSL 1.20; the bias is WZ_MIP_LOAD_BIAS, -0.5 with the default LOD distance setting
("High", lodDistanceBias -50). Mesa's nv30 compiles a biased lookup to the RSX's TXB, which samples
wrong whatever the bias: on the PS3 the whole 3D view was dark and flat while the UI (texture2D
without bias) was right. A shader mod drawing the same lookups as TEX and as TXB in stripes showed
it (2026-10-20). On the GLSL 1.20 path the macro is now texture2D(tex, uv): a plain lookup on every
driver, at the cost of the LOD distance setting (the -0.5 sharpening) on that path. Mesa patch 0045
fixes the driver side too; this keeps the game right with a Mesa without it.

---
diff --git a/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp b/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
--- a/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
+++ b/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
@@ -1148,6 +1148,17 @@
 			{
 				patchFragmentShaderTextureLodBias(fragmentShaderStr, mipLodBias.value());
 			}
+			{
+				// GLSL 1.20 shaders sample through texture2D(tex, uv, bias): drop the bias argument for
+				// a plain lookup (Mesa's nv30 turns the biased one into the RSX's TXB, which samples wrong
+				// whatever the bias: the PS3's 3D view was dark); the LOD distance setting is lost there
+				const std::string biasMacro = "#define texture(tex,uv,bias) texture2D(tex,uv,bias)";
+				size_t pos = fragmentShaderStr.find(biasMacro);
+				if (pos != std::string::npos)
+				{
+					fragmentShaderStr.replace(pos, biasMacro.size(), "#define texture(tex,uv,bias) texture2D(tex,uv)");
+				}
+			}
 
 			const char* ShaderStrings[2] = { fragment_header, fragmentShaderStr.c_str() };
 
